---

<DocShell
   title="Release checklist"
   summary="Public releases need one last reality check. CI covers the fast, repeatable virtual path. It does not replace real assistive technology smoke tests."
   links={links}
>
   <section>
      <h2>Before a public minor or major release</h2>
      <ol>
         <li>Wait for all CI checks to pass.</li>
         <li>Run a manual macOS VoiceOver smoke pass on representative fixtures or demo targets.</li>
         <li>Run a manual Windows NVDA smoke pass on representative fixtures or demo targets.</li>
         <li>Record what was exercised and any environment constraints that mattered.</li>
      </ol>
   </section>

   <section class="callout">
      <h2>Why this page exists</h2>
      <p>
         VoiceOver and NVDA are the real target platforms. The virtual reader is valuable, but it is not
         a substitute for shipping confidence on those platforms.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
